psim2 is distributed under the Eclipse Public License 2.0. See LICENSE.

This project adapts microscopic simulation algorithms from Eclipse SUMO 1.28.0.
Eclipse SUMO is copyright (C) 2001-2026 German Aerospace Center (DLR) and others.
The C++ modules identify their upstream models, including MSVehicle, MSLane,
the car-following and lane-change models, pedestrian striping, rail signals,
routing and traffic-light logic. The parallel scheduling and simulation state
layout are specific to psim2. Upstream source and notices:
https://github.com/eclipse-sumo/sumo/tree/v1_28_0

The traction and resistance curves and train parameters in psim2/railtypes.hpp
derive from MSCFModel_Rail.h, copyright (C) 2012-2026 German Aerospace Center
(DLR) and others. The generator preserves the original license notice.

The BeST v2 Berlin traffic scenario from DCAITI, Technische Universität
Berlin, was used for external validation. The scenario is available separately
under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International.
https://www.dcaiti.tu-berlin.de/research/simulation/downloads/get/best-scenario-v2.zip
